        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most people the best treadmill with iFIT is the NordicTrack Commercial 1750</strong>:
            a 22-inch belt, a decline for route workouts, a 400 lb rating and a screen that pivots for
            classes off the belt. For a touchscreen under $1,000, buy the T Series 10; for the lowest
            price, the T Series 5 with your own tablet; for a ProForm, the Carbon TLX, or the Pro 2000
            if you want decline; and for speed and the biggest screen, the Commercial 2450.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, decide on the membership before you decide on the treadmill, because
            it can cost more than the machine over its life. If you are unsure whether you will keep
            paying, read our guide to
            <a href="/is-ifit-worth-it/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">whether iFIT is worth it</a>
            first.
          </p>
